  "title": "When a sector's big names move, its smaller names catch up the next day",
  "why": "News about an industry reaches its most-followed stocks first; the smaller ones in the same sector take it in over the following day or two (Hou 2007; Lo and MacKinlay 1990). So rank the less-traded names by how far their sector's leaders moved today, or by how far they lag those leaders, and hold a day or two.",
